      "sourceTextSha256": "258695d3b4015e8c1aafd8d1678fc44ce35e47d175f533b038792fe4ad0405d0",
      "text": "After breakfast, you will join a group excursion to Montevideo with an English-speaking guide. Ferry tickets are included.\n\nMontevideo, Uruguay's capital and largest city, was founded in 1724. The sightseeing programme begins at Independence Square and the monument to national hero José Artigas. The route then follows Avenida 18 de Julio to the Parliament building.\n\nDuring the tour, you will visit a market to discover local produce and cuisine. You will then see the Prado district, with its parks, rose gardens and early 20th-century mansions designed by European architects. Along the way is Centenario Stadium, associated with the first Football World Cup.\n\nThe final part of the route takes you through Carrasco and Punta Gorda and along the Rambla waterfront beside the beaches. After the excursion, return to Buenos Aires.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw376c69-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "Verified Word paragraphs 78–80 contain a more specific Mercado Agrícola visit and French/Italian architects, but no matching passage with the RU description of discovering local cuisine and its general European-architect wording. Translate the full pinned RU block without adding Word-only duration or specifics."
      }
